INT. VILLAGE CHURCH - WEDDING - DAY

Pews packed. Organ droning. A banner reading CONGRATS ROSALIND & FERDINAND, slightly crooked.

At the altar: BRIDE ROSALIND, thirties, in a dress with a train like a snow drift. GROOM FERDINAND, thirties, sweating through a rented tux. FATHER MALACHY, sixties, bearded officiant, clutching a prayer book. In the front pew, MOTHER IRENE, sixties, in a hat the size of a satellite dish. Beside Ferdinand: BEST MAN, twenties, hungover, swaying.

FATHER MALACHY
If anyone objects to this union, speak now.

A pause. The BEST MAN raises a hand.

BEST MAN
Hang on.

ROSALIND
Oh, for God's sake.

BEST MAN
I just wanted to say I love you both.

FERDINAND
Thank you, Gideon.

The Best Man, now GIDEON, beams.

Over the church speakers, a booming voice.

DJ (V.O.)
(over PA)
Ladies and gentlemen, give it up for the happy couple!

FATHER MALACHY
We're not there yet!

MOTHER IRENE
(standing)
Who hired that man?

ROSALIND
Mother!

DJ (V.O.)
(over PA)
Drop the bass!

A thump rattles the pews. Everyone ducks.

GIDEON
(slurring)
Best. Day. Ever.

FERDINAND
Rosalind, I do. I do. Can we just finish?

ROSALIND
Fine. I do!

FATHER MALACHY
You may now--

The organ explodes into a dance remix. Everyone throws up their hands.
